  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ICT Transforming Education in Africa - Phase III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The third phase of the ICT Transforming Education in Africa project is a 4-year, USD 4 million initiative dedicated to advancing education in Namibia, Tanzania, and Uganda through the establishment of technology-enabled open school systems. Building on the success of previous project phases, it prioritizes digital inclusion, mainstreaming digital skills, fostering pedagogical transformation, supporting ICT and digital learning policy development, and strengthening teachers&apos; capacities.</narrative>
  </description>
